1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:09,230
[Forbidden, villains]

2
00:00:17,550 --> 00:00:19,130
Hi, good morning.

3
00:00:22,570 --> 00:00:23,750
Get up.

4
00:00:29,830 --> 00:00:32,770
I hope today will be a good day too.

5
00:00:32,860 --> 00:00:34,840
May everything go well.

6
00:00:35,020 --> 00:00:37,000
Thank you, Heaven and Earth.

7
00:00:37,880 --> 00:00:39,200
Hsieh Tien-ti.

8
00:00:39,290 --> 00:00:42,320
How far is your new home from the office?

9
00:00:42,410 --> 00:00:44,790
It's a little far.

10
00:00:44,870 --> 00:00:48,350
But that place has great feng shui.

11
00:00:48,480 --> 00:00:49,850
Plus,

12
00:00:49,930 --> 00:00:50,770
my favorite

13
00:00:50,860 --> 00:00:53,500
is the road that I can see
from the balcony.

14
00:00:53,580 --> 00:00:55,610
It's lined with trees.

15
00:00:55,780 --> 00:00:58,250
Think about it.

16
00:00:58,380 --> 00:01:01,150
It will be even more beautiful
during fall.

17
00:01:01,240 --> 00:01:02,160
Knowing that

18
00:01:02,250 --> 00:01:03,750
I'll pass by that road every day

19
00:01:03,880 --> 00:01:05,950
makes me feel great.

20
00:01:09,600 --> 00:01:11,180
Get up.

21
00:01:18,800 --> 00:01:21,700
The sun is too strong.

22
00:01:25,880 --> 00:01:27,820
Good morning, Ai-ting, Ai-yu.

23
00:01:27,900 --> 00:01:29,050
Good morning.

24
00:01:29,140 --> 00:01:30,940
Hi.

25
00:01:31,070 --> 00:01:32,520
Where's grandma?

26
00:01:32,610 --> 00:01:34,720
You'll go to school by yourselves today?

27
00:01:34,810 --> 00:01:37,009
Grandma...

28
00:01:37,100 --> 00:01:40,180
My grandma is sick,
so she's resting at home.

29
00:01:40,310 --> 00:01:41,539
Say goodbye to the lady.

30
00:01:41,630 --> 00:01:43,000
Bye, miss.

31
00:01:43,080 --> 00:01:44,539
Bye.

32
00:01:50,830 --> 00:01:51,530
Don't you think those two

33
00:01:51,620 --> 00:01:53,470
are a little strange today?

34
00:01:53,550 --> 00:01:55,090
I think so too.

35
00:01:56,460 --> 00:01:57,729
Come on.

36
00:01:59,630 --> 00:02:02,000
I don't want to go to work.

37
00:02:02,130 --> 00:02:03,010
Serves you right.

38
00:02:03,100 --> 00:02:04,640
I'm so tired.

39
00:02:05,350 --> 00:02:06,970
Grandma is missing.

40
00:02:07,110 --> 00:02:08,509
Why did you lie to them

41
00:02:08,600 --> 00:02:11,550
and say grandma is sick
and resting at home?

42
00:02:13,220 --> 00:02:16,570
Ai-yu, I'm sure Grandma just went to work.

43
00:02:16,650 --> 00:02:19,470
She wouldn't just leave
without telling us.

44
00:02:19,560 --> 00:02:21,850
Here. Grandma will accompany you.

45
00:02:23,340 --> 00:02:24,490
Put this on.

46
00:02:29,150 --> 00:02:30,870
Now, listen to me.

47
00:02:31,000 --> 00:02:32,320
Be good in school.

48
00:02:32,410 --> 00:02:34,780
Grandma will be waiting for you at home.

49
00:02:34,870 --> 00:02:36,230
Okay.

50
00:02:37,910 --> 00:02:38,960
Smile.

51
00:02:39,050 --> 00:02:41,120
Little Ai-yu, let's get to class.

52
00:02:41,200 --> 00:02:42,440
Say goodbye to your sister.

53
00:02:42,520 --> 00:02:43,710
Bye-bye, Ai-ting.

54
00:02:43,800 --> 00:02:45,210
Bye.

55
00:02:45,340 --> 00:02:46,700
-Let's go.
-Be good.

56
00:02:46,880 --> 00:02:48,380
We're late.

57
00:03:00,170 --> 00:03:01,140
Hello?

58
00:03:01,220 --> 00:03:02,980
I'm Hsieh Tien-ti from Mountain Travel.

59
00:03:05,930 --> 00:03:07,520
Aunt Su-chen?

60
00:03:08,440 --> 00:03:10,240
Why are you calling the office?

61
00:03:10,330 --> 00:03:13,370
No, I was too busy this week.

62
00:03:13,460 --> 00:03:15,440
I was going to call you back
when I was available.

63
00:03:15,570 --> 00:03:16,710
But...

64
00:03:16,840 --> 00:03:18,820
Yes, I've been too busy.

65
00:03:18,910 --> 00:03:21,240
I'm leading a tour this Saturday.

66
00:03:21,380 --> 00:03:22,920
I have work on Sunday too.

67
00:03:23,000 --> 00:03:24,680
Why about this?

68
00:03:24,760 --> 00:03:26,079
Since it has been a while
since my brother came back,

69
00:03:26,220 --> 00:03:28,280
you guys can dine together first
without me.

70
00:03:28,370 --> 00:03:29,560
Bye.

71
00:03:33,560 --> 00:03:34,750
What are you looking at?

72
00:03:35,940 --> 00:03:38,310
You're free on Saturday and Sunday.

73
00:03:38,400 --> 00:03:39,940
Why did you lie to Aunt Su-chen?

74
00:03:40,030 --> 00:03:42,050
Tell me. Who are you going out with?

75
00:03:43,020 --> 00:03:45,350
I just haven't written it down.

76
00:03:45,440 --> 00:03:46,100
It's my business.

77
00:03:46,230 --> 00:03:47,329
Do I have to tell you everything?

78
00:03:47,420 --> 00:03:48,390
Of course.

79
00:03:48,480 --> 00:03:49,270
I'm your roommate.

80
00:03:49,400 --> 00:03:50,850
We sleep in the same room.

81
00:03:50,940 --> 00:03:52,970
I'm meeting a vendor. I'm going out.

82
00:03:53,850 --> 00:03:55,120
Come back early.

83
00:03:59,350 --> 00:04:02,030
[Incoming call: Aunt Su-chen]

84
00:04:02,120 --> 00:04:02,870
[Aunt Su-chen]

85
00:04:02,290 --> 00:04:04,320
[I'm sorry, Aunt Su-chen.]

86
00:04:02,950 --> 00:04:03,310
[Missed call from Aunt Su-chen]

87
00:04:03,390 --> 00:04:10,700
[Tien-ti]

88
00:04:04,450 --> 00:04:06,520
[I'm in a meeting,
so I can't answer the phone.]

89
00:04:06,610 --> 00:04:08,670
Hello, Li-ting's mom. It's me, Ai-ting.

90
00:04:08,760 --> 00:04:10,080
When you picked her up from school today,

91
00:04:10,210 --> 00:04:12,060
did you see Ai-yu?

92
00:04:12,190 --> 00:04:13,290
Okay. If there's any news,

93
00:04:13,430 --> 00:04:14,790
please let me know.

94
00:04:14,880 --> 00:04:16,510
Thank you.

95
00:04:17,300 --> 00:04:18,709
Ai-ting.

96
00:04:18,790 --> 00:04:20,329
What's wrong?

97
00:04:20,420 --> 00:04:21,790
My sister is missing.

98
00:04:21,870 --> 00:04:23,900
Missing?

99
00:04:23,980 --> 00:04:25,300
How could she be missing?

100
00:04:25,440 --> 00:04:26,800
I don't know.

101
00:04:26,980 --> 00:04:28,250
When I went to fetch her
at the kindergarten today,

102
00:04:28,340 --> 00:04:29,530
she wasn't there.

103
00:04:29,620 --> 00:04:30,850
I've been going around the area.

104
00:04:30,980 --> 00:04:32,780
I couldn't find her anywhere.

105
00:04:34,020 --> 00:04:35,820
Then...

106
00:04:35,909 --> 00:04:38,330
How about you add me first?

107
00:04:38,460 --> 00:04:39,909
Send me your sister's photo.

108
00:04:40,000 --> 00:04:42,070
It will be faster
if we look for her together.

109
00:04:42,159 --> 00:04:43,430
Okay.

110
00:04:45,020 --> 00:04:46,820
Did you call your grandma to check?

111
00:04:46,909 --> 00:04:49,720
Maybe your grandma picked her up.

112
00:04:49,810 --> 00:04:51,180
No way.

113
00:04:53,640 --> 00:04:56,020
My grandma hasn't been coming home lately.

114
00:04:58,740 --> 00:05:00,370
I'll send you the photo.

115
00:05:00,460 --> 00:05:01,650
Okay.

116
00:05:01,740 --> 00:05:04,200
It's okay. Let's find your sister first.

117
00:05:07,500 --> 00:05:08,950
Don't worry.

118
00:05:09,920 --> 00:05:13,310
I'm good at finding people.

119
00:05:15,020 --> 00:05:16,960
Is this the little girl who's lost?

120
00:05:17,050 --> 00:05:19,330
That's right. I asked where she lives

121
00:05:19,420 --> 00:05:21,310
and whether she remembers
her family's phone number.

122
00:05:21,400 --> 00:05:23,470
But she wouldn't say anything.

123
00:05:23,600 --> 00:05:25,580
It's okay. I'll handle the rest.

124
00:05:25,670 --> 00:05:27,030
Thank you, officer.

125
00:05:27,170 --> 00:05:28,050
No worries.

126
00:05:28,130 --> 00:05:29,230
Bye.

127
00:05:36,100 --> 00:05:37,640
Let's go. I'll take you home.

128
00:05:37,770 --> 00:05:39,659
You're not the police.

129
00:05:39,750 --> 00:05:42,390
Why did she call you "officer"?

130
00:05:42,520 --> 00:05:44,850
Who are you?

131
00:05:45,780 --> 00:05:47,320
I'm not human.

132
00:05:47,409 --> 00:05:48,770
I'm a Kawas.

133
00:05:48,860 --> 00:05:50,620
Kawas?

134
00:05:52,070 --> 00:05:53,920
You know what?

135
00:05:54,010 --> 00:05:58,540
Kids who don't listen to me
will go to the underworld.

136
00:05:58,630 --> 00:06:00,520
All right. Hold my hand.

137
00:06:11,560 --> 00:06:14,420
Hold onto the rabbit's ear.

138
00:06:14,550 --> 00:06:15,830
Make sure you don't touch me.

139
00:06:21,110 --> 00:06:25,460
♫ Come on, come on ♫

140
00:06:25,600 --> 00:06:28,020
-♫ Let me hear you ♫
-Let's go. Your sister is looking for you.

141
00:06:29,380 --> 00:06:33,650
♫ Come on, come on ♫

142
00:06:33,740 --> 00:06:37,650
♫ Let me see you ♫

143
00:06:37,740 --> 00:06:41,740
♫ Come on, come on ♫

144
00:06:41,830 --> 00:06:44,380
♫ Right at this moment ♫

145
00:06:44,520 --> 00:06:45,620
Miss.

146
00:06:45,750 --> 00:06:48,040
It's okay. I'll look for her myself.

147
00:06:49,659 --> 00:06:51,600
It worked yesterday though.

148
00:06:52,570 --> 00:06:53,930
Ai-ting.

149
00:06:56,570 --> 00:06:57,760
Let's look around a bit more.

150
00:06:57,850 --> 00:06:59,610
If we still can't find her,

151
00:06:59,740 --> 00:07:00,930
I'll go with you to the police.

152
00:07:01,060 --> 00:07:02,470
No.

153
00:07:02,600 --> 00:07:04,400
We can't call the police.

154
00:07:04,490 --> 00:07:06,600
Why can't we call the police?

155
00:07:06,690 --> 00:07:07,970
If I call the police,

156
00:07:08,050 --> 00:07:08,800
my sister and I

157
00:07:08,890 --> 00:07:10,610
might not be able to see each other again.

158
00:07:12,500 --> 00:07:13,770
Why would that be?

159
00:07:16,410 --> 00:07:18,220
What do you mean?

160
00:07:19,800 --> 00:07:23,060
Because Grandma is not our real grandma.

161
00:07:24,640 --> 00:07:26,360
She's not your real grandma?

162
00:07:27,330 --> 00:07:29,530
Then how did you end up living with her?

163
00:07:31,240 --> 00:07:34,630
My mom took us to Grandma's last year.

164
00:07:34,720 --> 00:07:36,260
She said she had an emergency.

165
00:07:36,350 --> 00:07:39,210
She asked us to wait for her at Grandma's.

166
00:07:39,290 --> 00:07:41,010
Then...

167
00:07:41,100 --> 00:07:43,250
she never returned.

168
00:07:45,100 --> 00:07:46,990
Grandma is a good person.

169
00:07:47,080 --> 00:07:49,020
She didn't kick us out.

170
00:07:49,110 --> 00:07:51,480
Instead, she took care of us until now.

171
00:07:52,630 --> 00:07:54,030
I looked it up on the Internet.

172
00:07:54,120 --> 00:07:56,360
If people find out about our family,

173
00:07:56,450 --> 00:07:57,460
my sister and I will be sent

174
00:07:57,550 --> 00:07:59,930
to different foster homes.

175
00:08:00,020 --> 00:08:01,860
I don't want to part with my sister.

176
00:08:01,950 --> 00:08:03,930
That's why we can't call the police.

177
00:08:15,500 --> 00:08:17,220
Ai-ting.

178
00:08:18,580 --> 00:08:20,210
I know how you feel.

179
00:08:20,340 --> 00:08:22,850
When I was young,

180
00:08:22,940 --> 00:08:25,890
I was sent to a foster home too.

181
00:08:28,220 --> 00:08:31,560
I know what it's like to be separated
from your family.

182
00:08:31,650 --> 00:08:35,130
I felt like I was the only one left
in the world.

183
00:08:38,250 --> 00:08:40,140
That is why

184
00:08:40,230 --> 00:08:41,330
we have to get

185
00:08:41,419 --> 00:08:43,400
your family back.

186
00:08:49,600 --> 00:08:51,800
I'll take care of my family business.

187
00:08:51,890 --> 00:08:53,250
Please don't call the police.

188
00:08:53,340 --> 00:08:54,570
But if we don't call the police,

189
00:08:54,710 --> 00:08:57,080
we won't be able to solve the problem.

190
00:08:58,710 --> 00:09:00,690
You said you were sent to a foster home,

191
00:09:00,820 --> 00:09:02,010
right?

192
00:09:02,100 --> 00:09:03,420
After that,

193
00:09:03,550 --> 00:09:05,790
did you see your family again?

194
00:09:11,560 --> 00:09:13,540
Thank you for your kindness.

195
00:09:13,630 --> 00:09:15,430
I'll find my sister myself.

196
00:09:18,380 --> 00:09:19,430
Ai-ting.

197
00:09:33,780 --> 00:09:35,140
Ai-ting!

198
00:09:35,230 --> 00:09:36,860
Ai-yu!

199
00:09:36,950 --> 00:09:38,530
Where have you been?

200
00:09:38,620 --> 00:09:41,480
He took me back.

201
00:09:41,560 --> 00:09:43,100
Why did you follow a stranger?

202
00:09:43,190 --> 00:09:43,940
Didn't I tell you

203
00:09:44,030 --> 00:09:46,050
to wait for me after school?

204
00:09:50,630 --> 00:09:52,300
I'm sorry.

205
00:09:53,050 --> 00:09:54,280
You scared me.

206
00:09:54,370 --> 00:09:56,300
Don't do it again. Do you hear me?

207
00:09:56,390 --> 00:09:57,710
Yes.

208
00:10:07,790 --> 00:10:09,810
[You said you were sent to a foster home,]

209
00:10:09,940 --> 00:10:11,180
right?

210
00:10:11,260 --> 00:10:12,580
After that,

211
00:10:12,670 --> 00:10:14,960
did you see your family again?

212
00:10:39,380 --> 00:10:40,130
Mom.

213
00:10:42,900 --> 00:10:44,350
She's your sister from now on.

214
00:10:44,440 --> 00:10:45,710
Take care of her.

215
00:10:48,090 --> 00:10:49,370
Tien-ti.

216
00:10:49,500 --> 00:10:51,210
From now on, this will be your home.

217
00:10:51,300 --> 00:10:53,110
He's your older brother.

218
00:11:05,910 --> 00:11:06,660
[No matter how busy you are,]

219
00:11:06,750 --> 00:11:08,950
[don't forget to eat.]

220
00:11:18,670 --> 00:11:20,470
[Thank you, Aunt Su-chen.]

221
00:11:20,650 --> 00:11:22,500
[I've been busy.]

222
00:11:22,630 --> 00:11:26,060
[Let's have dinner when I have time.]

223
00:11:34,330 --> 00:11:36,490
Little Ai-yu.

224
00:11:36,580 --> 00:11:38,780
Where did you find her yesterday?

225
00:11:38,860 --> 00:11:41,940
Find her? Why would I be looking for her?

226
00:11:42,080 --> 00:11:45,680
Have you forgotten?
I helped you look for her yesterday.

227
00:11:45,770 --> 00:11:47,710
She was at home all day yesterday.

228
00:11:47,800 --> 00:11:49,780
Did you get it wrong?

229
00:11:49,860 --> 00:11:51,270
No.

230
00:11:51,450 --> 00:11:53,030
Didn't we look for her together yesterday?

231
00:11:53,120 --> 00:11:54,880
I even asked you
if we should call the police.

232
00:11:54,970 --> 00:11:56,600
You said we mustn't

233
00:11:56,680 --> 00:11:59,630
because Grandma was missing too, right?

234
00:11:59,760 --> 00:12:01,260
Grandma?

235
00:12:01,440 --> 00:12:03,330
We don't have a grandma.

236
00:12:03,420 --> 00:12:05,700
We don't have a grandma.

237
00:12:06,800 --> 00:12:08,650
You don't have a grandma?

238
00:12:12,170 --> 00:12:13,490
We should go.

239
00:12:13,580 --> 00:12:14,590
Say goodbye to the lady.

240
00:12:14,680 --> 00:12:16,040
Bye, miss.

241
00:12:25,500 --> 00:12:27,260
We're here, Mom.

242
00:12:31,530 --> 00:12:32,980
Okay.

243
00:12:35,180 --> 00:12:37,560
Okay, we'll talk later.

244
00:12:37,690 --> 00:12:38,830
Yes.

245
00:12:49,480 --> 00:12:51,640
Yesterday...

246
00:12:55,690 --> 00:12:57,490
I can't have remembered wrongly.

247
00:12:58,460 --> 00:12:59,210
[How about you add me first?]

248
00:12:59,290 --> 00:13:00,660
Send me your sister's photo.

249
00:13:00,750 --> 00:13:02,200
It will be faster
if we look for her together.

250
00:13:03,170 --> 00:13:04,710
Okay.

251
00:13:06,110 --> 00:13:07,480
The photo.

252
00:13:15,750 --> 00:13:18,830
Thank God I reacted quickly.

253
00:13:21,560 --> 00:13:24,810
What was I looking for?

254
00:13:24,940 --> 00:13:26,750
Why can't I remember?

255
00:13:44,880 --> 00:13:47,340
What is this place?

256
00:13:48,220 --> 00:13:50,860
A place where no one will find you.

257
00:13:52,360 --> 00:13:53,940
Stay here quietly.

258
00:13:54,070 --> 00:13:55,790
When all the Kawas are gone,

259
00:13:55,880 --> 00:13:56,840
I'll do as promised

260
00:13:56,980 --> 00:13:58,870
and take you
to your precious granddaughters.

261
00:14:03,350 --> 00:14:04,980
Right.

262
00:14:06,520 --> 00:14:08,060
Everything here is great.

263
00:14:08,190 --> 00:14:09,380
But the sun is a bit too strong.

264
00:14:09,560 --> 00:14:10,880
Don't get burned.

265
00:14:57,120 --> 00:14:59,010
When are you going to change

266
00:14:59,140 --> 00:15:02,400
this bad habit of trespassing
into other people's turf?

267
00:15:03,850 --> 00:15:07,280
Do I do that? I don't seem to recall.

268
00:15:08,120 --> 00:15:09,620
Don't be smart with me.

269
00:15:09,700 --> 00:15:12,120
You know what I'm talking about.

270
00:15:12,260 --> 00:15:13,750
Hand over Raka.

271
00:15:21,230 --> 00:15:23,340
Kakarayan has arranged everything.

272
00:15:23,430 --> 00:15:25,460
Before the last rainfall,

273
00:15:25,540 --> 00:15:28,620
He wants to evacuate all the spirits
from the mortal world.

274
00:15:28,710 --> 00:15:30,250
Not a single one less.

275
00:15:30,340 --> 00:15:32,980
Don't get in my way now.

276
00:15:33,070 --> 00:15:33,950
I'm more curious

277
00:15:34,080 --> 00:15:35,620
if this is Kakarayan's instruction

278
00:15:35,710 --> 00:15:37,340
or is it your own plan?

279
00:15:37,420 --> 00:15:38,790
Because what you just said

280
00:15:38,880 --> 00:15:40,680
seems to be a little different

281
00:15:40,810 --> 00:15:42,530
from what I saw in the Reflection of Time.

282
00:15:57,930 --> 00:16:00,610
[Mountain Travel]

283
00:16:02,550 --> 00:16:03,780
Did you receive it?

284
00:16:03,910 --> 00:16:05,100
What?

285
00:16:09,150 --> 00:16:10,820
Hsieh Tien-ti.

286
00:16:10,950 --> 00:16:12,930
Why are you redoing the tour report?

287
00:16:13,020 --> 00:16:14,290
What?

288
00:16:14,380 --> 00:16:16,580
You told me to do this last time.

289
00:16:16,670 --> 00:16:18,690
The one when Ms. Amamiya got lost.

290
00:16:18,780 --> 00:16:20,370
Did you forget?

291
00:16:23,930 --> 00:16:25,510
Now, you remember.

292
00:16:25,600 --> 00:16:27,140
It's time to go home. I'm so hungry.

293
00:16:27,270 --> 00:16:28,680
Come eat with me.

294
00:16:28,510 --> 00:16:42,940
[Mountain Travel]

295
00:16:30,400 --> 00:16:31,890
Lock the door later, do you hear me?

296
00:16:31,980 --> 00:16:33,790
Okay, bye.

297
00:16:34,580 --> 00:16:37,130
What's wrong with my head these days?

298
00:16:37,220 --> 00:16:39,590
I'm so forgetful these days.

299
00:16:39,680 --> 00:16:41,310
It's because you bought a house.

300
00:16:41,400 --> 00:16:43,950
That's why you're exhausted.

301
00:16:44,040 --> 00:16:45,220
I have an idea.

302
00:16:45,310 --> 00:16:47,250
Perhaps you could get a man
who owns a house?

303
00:16:47,340 --> 00:16:49,400
You can relax then.

304
00:16:49,490 --> 00:16:53,010
Forget it. I have no taste in men.

305
00:16:54,420 --> 00:16:56,180
I always meet the worst kind.

306
00:16:58,030 --> 00:17:01,900
I think so too, judging from your exes.

307
00:17:01,990 --> 00:17:03,790
It's more practical to eat rice.

308
00:17:03,880 --> 00:17:04,980
I'm famished.

309
00:17:35,470 --> 00:17:37,230
You are...

310
00:17:42,910 --> 00:17:45,020
From now on,

311
00:17:45,110 --> 00:17:47,390
you'll forget you ever saw me.

312
00:17:47,480 --> 00:17:51,310
Forget about helping Chen Ai-ting
look for her sister last night.

313
00:17:51,400 --> 00:17:53,470
You'll forget everything

314
00:17:53,550 --> 00:17:55,750
and return to your previous life.

315
00:18:22,110 --> 00:18:25,280
[Delete the photo?]

316
00:18:34,960 --> 00:18:37,820
How many times have I told you?

317
00:18:37,900 --> 00:18:40,900
Watch where you're going.

318
00:18:40,980 --> 00:18:42,610
You bumbling fool.

319
00:18:51,370 --> 00:18:54,320
Thank God I reacted quickly.

320
00:18:57,180 --> 00:19:00,390
What was I looking for?

321
00:19:00,480 --> 00:19:02,460
[Why can't I remember?]

322
00:19:08,090 --> 00:19:09,280
Students.

323
00:19:09,360 --> 00:19:11,390
Let me ask you a question.

324
00:19:11,480 --> 00:19:13,460
Who believes that the world we live in

325
00:19:13,540 --> 00:19:14,690
was created by God?

326
00:19:14,860 --> 00:19:16,180
Raise your hand.

327
00:19:18,300 --> 00:19:19,570
No one does?

328
00:19:19,700 --> 00:19:20,630
Okay.

329
00:19:20,710 --> 00:19:22,910
Let's move on to another question.

330
00:19:21,950 --> 00:19:24,500
[Doomsday?]

331
00:19:23,000 --> 00:19:26,040
Let's say a car was parked
on the beach today.

332
00:19:26,130 --> 00:19:28,590
Do you think someone
left it there on purpose?

333
00:19:28,680 --> 00:19:30,480
Or did it appear there

334
00:19:30,570 --> 00:19:32,950
out of nowhere?

335
00:19:33,030 --> 00:19:34,490
Professor.

336
00:19:34,570 --> 00:19:36,470
Someone must have parked it there.

337
00:19:36,550 --> 00:19:38,230
Why can you believe someone parked it

338
00:19:38,360 --> 00:19:40,030
on the beach

339
00:19:40,120 --> 00:19:43,020
but don't believe that God
created this world?

340
00:19:43,150 --> 00:19:44,610
You should study more.

341
00:19:46,590 --> 00:19:47,420
Professor.

342
00:19:47,510 --> 00:19:49,010
A car's structure is complicated.

343
00:19:49,140 --> 00:19:50,500
It couldn't have appeared out of nowhere.

344
00:19:50,590 --> 00:19:52,130
Someone must have parked it on the beach.

345
00:19:52,220 --> 00:19:53,360
Don't you realize this world's structure

346
00:19:53,450 --> 00:19:55,870
is much more complicated than a car?

347
00:19:55,960 --> 00:19:58,250
You trust that a car was built,

348
00:19:58,330 --> 00:19:59,170
but you don't believe

349
00:19:59,260 --> 00:20:01,990
that the world was created by God.

350
00:20:02,120 --> 00:20:03,350
You should study less.

351
00:20:05,420 --> 00:20:06,780
It's okay.

352
00:20:06,910 --> 00:20:09,070
To discuss whether gods exist or not

353
00:20:09,160 --> 00:20:10,700
is like discussing the end of the world.

354
00:20:10,790 --> 00:20:12,980
Same topic, different variations.

355
00:20:13,160 --> 00:20:14,170
Tell me.

356
00:20:14,260 --> 00:20:15,180
What are your thoughts

357
00:20:15,270 --> 00:20:17,560
on the end of the world?

358
00:20:18,700 --> 00:20:22,000
Professor, it should be something
like a meteorite colliding with the earth.

359
00:20:22,140 --> 00:20:23,540
No one will survive.

360
00:20:23,630 --> 00:20:25,170
What else?

361
00:20:25,260 --> 00:20:26,270
Professor.

362
00:20:26,360 --> 00:20:27,640
I think it will be like a movie.

363
00:20:27,720 --> 00:20:28,740
Due to biochemical weapons,

364
00:20:28,820 --> 00:20:30,450
humans will turn into zombies.

365
00:20:32,610 --> 00:20:35,200
That's a very creative answer.

366
00:20:35,290 --> 00:20:37,180
But I'm telling you,

367
00:20:37,270 --> 00:20:38,550
the real end of the world

368
00:20:38,640 --> 00:20:41,100
won't be as exciting as you think.

369
00:20:41,190 --> 00:20:43,390
Rather, it will be silent.

370
00:20:43,480 --> 00:20:45,100
Just like how Earth

371
00:20:45,190 --> 00:20:47,570
experienced three major
ecological extinctions in the past.

372
00:20:47,660 --> 00:20:50,160
It happened quietly each time.

373
00:20:51,790 --> 00:20:53,020
Who knows?

374
00:20:53,110 --> 00:20:54,480
The end of days

375
00:20:54,560 --> 00:20:56,320
has silently crept up behind you.

376
00:20:56,410 --> 00:20:57,290
Just like how you don't believe

377
00:20:57,380 --> 00:20:59,930
that gods exist in this world.

378
00:21:00,060 --> 00:21:01,690
Because you can't see it,

379
00:21:01,780 --> 00:21:04,420
you think the end hasn't come.

380
00:21:04,550 --> 00:21:06,840
But it's not that you don't see it.

381
00:21:06,970 --> 00:21:09,870
You're just overlooking its occurrence.

382
00:21:12,870 --> 00:21:15,420
Okay, that's all for today.

383
00:21:15,510 --> 00:21:16,780
Class dismissed.

384
00:21:20,040 --> 00:21:22,410
You jerk.
You're leaking classified information.

385
00:21:22,500 --> 00:21:24,000
If Kakarayan finds out,

386
00:21:24,090 --> 00:21:25,320
you're going to suffer.

387
00:21:25,410 --> 00:21:27,830
Be quiet.

388
00:21:27,910 --> 00:21:29,980
You'll get me killed.

389
00:21:30,860 --> 00:21:32,580
Let's go to our secret base.

390
00:21:32,670 --> 00:21:34,160
Come on.

391
00:21:37,240 --> 00:21:39,840
'Orad. Why are you here?

392
00:21:41,160 --> 00:21:42,920
I really don't get it.

393
00:21:43,010 --> 00:21:44,810
The Kawas that have been evacuated

394
00:21:44,900 --> 00:21:47,450
were told to leave

395
00:21:47,580 --> 00:21:48,810
because the deterioration
of the environment here

396
00:21:48,900 --> 00:21:50,710
is affecting their well-being.

397
00:21:50,790 --> 00:21:52,030
But me?

398
00:21:52,110 --> 00:21:54,090
I'm the god of wisdom.

399
00:21:54,180 --> 00:21:55,330
I worked so hard for thousands of years.

400
00:21:55,460 --> 00:21:57,260
I'm an educator.

401
00:21:57,390 --> 00:22:00,600
The more knowledgeable humans are,
the happier I'll be.

402
00:22:00,690 --> 00:22:02,230
Why should I leave?

403
00:22:02,360 --> 00:22:02,800
I don't get it.

404
00:22:02,940 --> 00:22:04,700
This is Kakarayan's plan.

405
00:22:04,830 --> 00:22:06,720
Nobody can oppose it.

406
00:22:08,080 --> 00:22:11,560
As for the knowledge
and wisdom you mentioned,

407
00:22:11,650 --> 00:22:12,700
those things will disappear

408
00:22:12,840 --> 00:22:15,870
along with the Kawas' retreat.

409
00:22:15,960 --> 00:22:17,410
Do you still think

410
00:22:17,500 --> 00:22:18,820
you'll be okay after that?

411
00:22:18,950 --> 00:22:19,920
Fine. Let's say that's true.

412
00:22:20,050 --> 00:22:21,020
I'll just worry about it

413
00:22:21,150 --> 00:22:22,470
when it actually happens.

414
00:22:22,560 --> 00:22:24,580
I told you, this is Kakarayan's plan.

415
00:22:24,670 --> 00:22:26,650
"Kakarayan's plan."

416
00:22:26,740 --> 00:22:27,750
Yes, you've said it twice.

417
00:22:27,840 --> 00:22:29,380
As the god of wisdom,

418
00:22:29,470 --> 00:22:31,800
you should know what's best.

419
00:22:33,870 --> 00:22:36,110
Yes, I know.

420
00:22:36,200 --> 00:22:37,210
Okay, I accept His decision.

421
00:22:37,300 --> 00:22:39,320
I'll just go then.

422
00:22:39,410 --> 00:22:42,140
But first, let's have a drink.

423
00:22:42,230 --> 00:22:44,380
Here's a toast

424
00:22:44,470 --> 00:22:46,410
to the mighty, all-powerful Kakarayan

425
00:22:46,500 --> 00:22:50,060
that nobody can oppose.

426
00:22:50,150 --> 00:22:52,650
No, thank you. I'm still working.

427
00:22:54,850 --> 00:22:56,440
When have you

428
00:22:56,530 --> 00:22:57,890
ever stopped working?

429
00:22:58,070 --> 00:22:58,900
It's only one sip.

430
00:22:59,080 --> 00:23:00,620
Are you that scared?

431
00:23:00,710 --> 00:23:02,070
Is your job to please Him?

432
00:23:02,160 --> 00:23:03,960
Do you want to write a report
to Him as well?

433
00:23:04,090 --> 00:23:05,410
No.

434
00:23:05,500 --> 00:23:07,310
Then drink up.

435
00:23:07,390 --> 00:23:08,050
Come on.

436
00:23:08,140 --> 00:23:09,990
But...

437
00:23:10,080 --> 00:23:11,220
In the Reflection of Time,

438
00:23:11,310 --> 00:23:13,070
I didn't see myself drinking.

439
00:23:13,160 --> 00:23:15,890
The Reflection of Time.

440
00:23:15,970 --> 00:23:19,320
'Orad, this is bad.

441
00:23:19,410 --> 00:23:21,690
You've learned how to lie
through your teeth.

442
00:23:21,780 --> 00:23:23,810
And you call yourself
Kakarayan's messenger?

443
00:23:23,890 --> 00:23:26,180
I think you're just His servant.

444
00:23:26,800 --> 00:23:28,210
No.

445
00:23:28,340 --> 00:23:30,190
You're not His servant.

446
00:23:30,320 --> 00:23:31,550
You are...

447
00:23:31,730 --> 00:23:33,840
His slave dog.

448
00:23:36,520 --> 00:23:38,460
The small kind.

449
00:23:38,550 --> 00:23:39,430
A Chihuahua.

450
00:23:39,560 --> 00:23:40,830
"I'm not 'Orad. I'm a dog.

451
00:23:40,920 --> 00:23:42,730
I can't drink it."

452
00:23:48,750 --> 00:23:51,660
Cheers!

453
00:23:51,740 --> 00:23:52,760
Everyone, listen up.

454
00:23:52,840 --> 00:23:55,310
We're celebrating
our good performance this month.

455
00:23:55,400 --> 00:23:59,660
It's a new record
since we started Mountain Travel.

456
00:24:00,460 --> 00:24:02,220
A new record!

457
00:24:02,300 --> 00:24:04,240
No one gets to go home

458
00:24:04,330 --> 00:24:06,480
if they're not stuffed and drunk.

459
00:24:06,620 --> 00:24:08,200
Okay!

460
00:24:10,140 --> 00:24:12,030
Ms. Chang-fen, I think you're too much.

461
00:24:12,160 --> 00:24:14,490
You bought a lot of alcohol.

462
00:24:14,580 --> 00:24:16,470
Go for it. I can't help you.

463
00:24:16,600 --> 00:24:17,790
Hsieh Tien-ti.

464
00:24:17,970 --> 00:24:18,980
You're such a killjoy.

465
00:24:19,160 --> 00:24:20,430
Pour the wine!

466
00:24:23,160 --> 00:24:25,050
Ms. Chang-fen, here's to you.

467
00:24:25,140 --> 00:24:26,060
Hold on.

468
00:24:26,150 --> 00:24:27,650
Okay, got it.

469
00:24:28,180 --> 00:24:30,900
Drink!

470
00:24:31,520 --> 00:24:33,590
It's not that I don't want to drink.

471
00:24:33,720 --> 00:24:35,350
I can't.

472
00:24:35,440 --> 00:24:37,590
Is it because

473
00:24:37,720 --> 00:24:39,220
when you're drunk,

474
00:24:39,350 --> 00:24:41,810
you sleep around?

475
00:24:42,830 --> 00:24:44,320
All right.

476
00:24:44,450 --> 00:24:46,960
I'll tell you since we're family now.

477
00:24:47,090 --> 00:24:49,160
This is the story.

478
00:24:49,290 --> 00:24:53,340
My body constitution is different
from ordinary people.

479
00:24:53,470 --> 00:24:54,570
Who is the same?

480
00:24:55,720 --> 00:24:57,520
You're right, Mom.

481
00:24:57,610 --> 00:24:58,360
Who is the same?

482
00:24:58,450 --> 00:25:01,170
When I drink,

483
00:25:01,260 --> 00:25:06,280
I'll see something

484
00:25:06,370 --> 00:25:09,010
that normal people can't see.

485
00:25:12,040 --> 00:25:12,920
I can't see.

486
00:25:13,050 --> 00:25:13,630
I can't see you.

487
00:25:13,760 --> 00:25:14,680
No, I can't.

488
00:25:14,810 --> 00:25:16,350
I can't see you.

489
00:25:16,490 --> 00:25:17,670
You can't see me either.

490
00:25:17,810 --> 00:25:18,950
It's true!

491
00:25:19,040 --> 00:25:20,050
I can't see you either.

492
00:25:20,140 --> 00:25:21,680
There was once when I was young,

493
00:25:21,770 --> 00:25:24,450
I secretly drank my grandma's wine.

494
00:25:24,540 --> 00:25:26,610
Then I...

495
00:25:27,270 --> 00:25:29,860
I saw a pair of red eyes.

496
00:25:33,640 --> 00:25:35,580
[At the time, I couldn't]

497
00:25:35,710 --> 00:25:37,910
[take a good look at the face.]

498
00:25:39,670 --> 00:25:42,970
[But I knew that those eyes]

499
00:25:43,060 --> 00:25:44,820
[were staring at me.]

500
00:25:47,990 --> 00:25:51,550
Hsieh Tien-ti,
you should be called a genius.

501
00:25:51,680 --> 00:25:52,700
You could write a drama.

502
00:25:52,830 --> 00:25:54,410
What a story.

503
00:25:56,040 --> 00:25:56,960
Bring me the wine.

504
00:25:57,050 --> 00:25:57,890
Here.

505
00:25:57,980 --> 00:25:59,080
That's mine.

506
00:25:59,250 --> 00:26:00,440
Listen to me.

507
00:26:01,280 --> 00:26:03,780
I'll make a toast to you.

508
00:26:03,870 --> 00:26:05,190
Just one sip.

509
00:26:05,320 --> 00:26:06,510
-No.
-One sip.

510
00:26:06,600 --> 00:26:07,960
Come on.

511
00:26:08,050 --> 00:26:09,420
One, two, three.

512
00:26:09,550 --> 00:26:10,470
Drink it.

513
00:26:10,560 --> 00:26:12,140
Drink.

514
00:26:12,280 --> 00:26:14,520
Okay, I'll drink it.

515
00:26:15,490 --> 00:26:17,120
I'll drink it!

516
00:26:17,200 --> 00:26:18,700
Listen up.

517
00:26:18,790 --> 00:26:19,800
If anything strange

518
00:26:19,890 --> 00:26:20,900
happens later,

519
00:26:20,990 --> 00:26:22,660
I already warned you.

520
00:26:22,750 --> 00:26:24,290
Okay.

521
00:26:25,120 --> 00:26:26,440
Go on.

522
00:26:29,130 --> 00:26:31,060
Okay, I'll drink it.

523
00:26:31,190 --> 00:26:32,470
I'll drink it.

524
00:27:07,100 --> 00:27:09,210
Do you see anything?

525
00:27:13,210 --> 00:27:14,360
No.

526
00:27:16,640 --> 00:27:18,010
You quack.

527
00:27:18,100 --> 00:27:19,420
Are you kidding me?

528
00:27:19,500 --> 00:27:21,000
Useless thing!

529
00:27:21,090 --> 00:27:22,360
Useless!

530
00:27:22,450 --> 00:27:23,820
You're still the best.

531
00:27:26,370 --> 00:27:28,000
Beer is in my coffee pot.

532
00:27:28,130 --> 00:27:28,790
Cheers.

533
00:27:28,920 --> 00:27:30,150
That's terrible.

534
00:27:30,280 --> 00:27:33,360
What's this? Give me the whole can.

535
00:27:33,500 --> 00:27:34,820
The whole can.

536
00:27:34,900 --> 00:27:36,580
Let's drink until we drop.

537
00:27:36,660 --> 00:27:38,030
Pu.

538
00:27:38,120 --> 00:27:39,220
Get me some pizza.

539
00:27:39,300 --> 00:27:40,760
Pizza.

540
00:27:41,940 --> 00:27:44,800
You're so lousy. You can't eat it?

541
00:27:44,940 --> 00:27:46,610
Have a drink.

542
00:27:48,760 --> 00:27:50,700
Hurry up.

543
00:27:51,760 --> 00:27:55,190
I'm dizzy.

544
00:27:56,510 --> 00:27:59,060
I shouldn't have drunk so much.

545
00:28:00,340 --> 00:28:02,710
What's so great about alcohol anyway?

546
00:28:10,590 --> 00:28:14,720
Grandma used to drink every day.

547
00:28:17,540 --> 00:28:20,000
She must have felt sick too.

548
00:28:29,150 --> 00:28:33,640
♫ Come on, come on ♫

549
00:28:45,040 --> 00:28:49,220
♫ Come on, come on ♫

550
00:28:49,310 --> 00:28:52,740
♫ Right at this moment ♫

551
00:28:52,830 --> 00:28:54,190
See?

552
00:28:54,280 --> 00:28:55,250
It's there.

553
00:28:57,580 --> 00:29:00,220
It's flying.

554
00:29:03,210 --> 00:29:05,010
Look over there.

555
00:29:05,100 --> 00:29:06,860
There are more.

556
00:29:08,580 --> 00:29:09,240
Look here.

557
00:29:09,370 --> 00:29:13,770
♫ Come on, come on ♫

558
00:29:13,860 --> 00:29:18,120
♫ Right at this moment ♫

559
00:29:18,210 --> 00:29:26,620
♫ Show yourself before me ♫

560
00:30:13,960 --> 00:30:15,540
[Who are you? How did you get in here?]

561
00:30:15,150 --> 00:30:37,150
[Next episode]

562
00:30:16,860 --> 00:30:17,790
You can see me?

563
00:30:17,870 --> 00:30:19,630
[Why does he seem so gentle]

564
00:30:19,720 --> 00:30:21,480
[from what I can remember?]

565
00:30:21,610 --> 00:30:22,980
[From now on,]

566
00:30:23,070 --> 00:30:24,870
[I will be your guardian angel.]

567
00:30:24,960 --> 00:30:27,160
[Because you know too much]

568
00:30:27,250 --> 00:30:28,610
of what you shouldn't.

569
00:30:28,740 --> 00:30:30,550
That's why it has come to this.

